{"name":"Sombrero Tan","hex":"#cba391","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sombrero","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of hat with a high conical or cylindrical crown and a saucer-shaped brim, highly embroidered, made of plush felt.","A mixed drink with coffee liqueur and cream."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sombrero"},{"term":"tan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["The trigonometric function tangent."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tangale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sombrero","blocks":[{"text":"A sombrero, sombrero de charro or sombrero jarano, is a type of wide-brimmed hat used to shield the face and eyes from the sun. It usually has a high, pointed crown; an extra-wide brim, that is slightly upturned at the edge; and a chin strap to hold it in place. It is strongly associated with the culture of Mexico."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/CharroHatsMAPDF.JPG/330px-CharroHatsMAPDF.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sombrero"},{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/De_Sambaygo_y_Mulata%2C_sale_Canilajo_-_Pintura_de_Castas_%28M%C3%A9xico%2C_1760%29.jpg/250px-De_Sambaygo_y_Mulata%2C_sale_Canilajo_-_Pintura_de_Castas_%28M%C3%A9xico%2C_1760%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/De_Sambaygo_y_Mulata%2C_